field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ecc283f-a6e2-5680-818e-066fc64745c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ecc283f-a6e2-5680-818e-066fc64745c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303134} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ab0df7-f64e-5225-a2be-146b547645a3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11bc6671-f60f-5e8a-924a-ddb4eef9ace3" :question/math-academy-id "q-332436" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{4}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 4-{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
